  <Pages>

    <Page url="/">
      <VStack padding="2rem" gap="1.5rem">
        <H1>Wrapping React components for XMLUI</H1>

        <Markdown><![CDATA[
## The problem

Every XMLUI component that wraps a React component needs a **renderer** — a function that bridges XMLUI markup to React props. Today, these renderers are written by hand.

For a component like **Slider**, that means ~40 lines of mechanical mapping code:

- Calling `extractValue` for each prop
- Calling `extractValue.asOptionalBoolean` for each boolean prop
- Calling `lookupEventHandler` for each event
- Calling `lookupSyncCallback` for each callback
- Manually forwarding plumbing like `className`, `registerComponentApi`, `updateState`, and `state.value`

This approach has two problems:

1. **Boilerplate.** The mapping code is tedious to write and review.

2. **Incomplete coverage.** Because every prop must be explicitly listed, props that the native React component already supports get silently dropped. The wrapper becomes a bottleneck that filters out capabilities.

## A first-pass solution

`wrapComponent` is a utility that generates the renderer automatically. You declare only the exceptions — which props are booleans, which are events, which need renaming — and everything else passes through by default.

## This demo

- **Slider** is the hand-written original (40-line renderer).
- **SliderW** uses `wrapComponent` (13 lines), wrapping the exact same `SliderNative.tsx`.

The **Slider and SliderW** page confirms they behave identically for all currently-wrapped features.

The **Slider vs SliderW** page shows what **SliderW** can do that **Slider** can't — native props like `inverted`, `title`, and `tabIndex` that the hand-written renderer never forwarded.
]]></Markdown>

        <ExpandableItem summary="wrapComponent source code">
          <Markdown><![CDATA[
```typescript
import React from "react";
import type { ComponentMetadata } from "../abstractions/ComponentDefs";
import type { ComponentRendererDef } from "../abstractions/RendererDefs";
import { createComponentRenderer } from "./renderers";

export type WrapComponentConfig = {
  booleans?: string[];
  numbers?: string[];
  strings?: string[];
  events?: string[] | Record<string, string>;
  callbacks?: string[] | Record<string, string>;
  rename?: Record<string, string>;
  exclude?: string[];
  stateful?: boolean;
};

function capitalize(s: string): string {
  return s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);
}

function normalizeEvents(
  events: string[] | Record<string, string> | undefined,
): Record<string, string> {
  if (!events) return {};
  if (Array.isArray(events)) {
    const result: Record<string, string> = {};
    for (const name of events) {
      result[name] = `on${capitalize(name)}`;
    }
    return result;
  }
  return events;
}

function normalizeCallbacks(
  callbacks: string[] | Record<string, string> | undefined,
): Record<string, string> {
  if (!callbacks) return {};
  if (Array.isArray(callbacks)) {
    const result: Record<string, string> = {};
    for (const name of callbacks) {
      result[name] = name;
    }
    return result;
  }
  return callbacks;
}

export function wrapComponent<TMd extends ComponentMetadata>(
  type: string,
  Component: React.ComponentType<any>,
  metadata: TMd,
  config: WrapComponentConfig = {},
): ComponentRendererDef {
  const eventMap = normalizeEvents(config.events);
  const callbackMap = normalizeCallbacks(config.callbacks);
  const renameMap = config.rename ?? {};
  const booleanSet = new Set(config.booleans ?? []);
  const numberSet = new Set(config.numbers ?? []);
  const stringSet = new Set(config.strings ?? []);
  const excludeSet = new Set(config.exclude ?? []);

  const specialProps = new Set([
    ...Object.keys(eventMap),
    ...Object.keys(callbackMap),
    "id",
  ]);

  const isStateful =
    config.stateful ??
    !!(metadata.props?.["initialValue"] || metadata.events?.["didChange"]);

  if (isStateful) {
    specialProps.add("initialValue");
  }

  return createComponentRenderer(type, metadata, (context) => {
    const {
      node, extractValue, lookupEventHandler, lookupSyncCallback,
      className, updateState, state, registerComponentApi,
    } = context;

    const props: Record<string, any> = {};

    // Always pass through XMLUI plumbing
    props.className = className;
    props.registerComponentApi = registerComponentApi;

    if (isStateful) {
      props.updateState = updateState;
      props.value = state.value;
      props.initialValue = extractValue(node.props?.initialValue);
    }

    // Events
    for (const [xmluiName, reactPropName] of Object.entries(eventMap)) {
      props[reactPropName] = lookupEventHandler(xmluiName);
    }

    // Sync callbacks
    for (const [xmluiName, reactPropName] of Object.entries(callbackMap)) {
      props[reactPropName] = lookupSyncCallback(node.props?.[xmluiName]);
    }

    // Forward all remaining node.props
    if (node.props) {
      for (const [key, rawValue] of Object.entries(node.props)) {
        if (specialProps.has(key)) continue;
        if (excludeSet.has(key)) continue;

        const reactKey = renameMap[key] ?? key;

        if (booleanSet.has(key)) {
          props[reactKey] = extractValue.asOptionalBoolean(rawValue);
        } else if (numberSet.has(key)) {
          props[reactKey] = extractValue.asOptionalNumber(rawValue);
        } else if (stringSet.has(key)) {
          props[reactKey] = extractValue.asOptionalString(rawValue);
        } else {
          props[reactKey] = extractValue(rawValue);
        }
      }
    }

    return <Component {...props} />;
  });
}
```
]]></Markdown>
        </ExpandableItem>

      </VStack>
    </Page>

    <Page url="/slider-and-sliderw">
      <VStack padding="2rem" gap="2rem">

        <H1>Slider and SliderW</H1>

        <Markdown>
Both components wrap the same `SliderNative.tsx` React component.
**Slider** uses a hand-written 40-line renderer.
**SliderW** uses `wrapComponent` (13 lines).
These tests confirm they behave identically for all currently-wrapped features.
        </Markdown>

        <!-- === Basic usage === -->
        <Card var.sliderVal="" var.sliderWVal="">
          <H2>Basic: default props</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider</Text>
              <Slider id="s1" onDidChange="{(v) => sliderVal = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sliderVal}</Text>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW</Text>
              <SliderW id="sw1" onDidChange="{(v) => sliderWVal = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sliderWVal}</Text>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === Custom range === -->
        <Card var.s2Val="" var.sw2Val="">
          <H2>Custom range: 0–100, step 10</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider</Text>
              <Slider id="s2" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="10"
                initialValue="50"
                onDidChange="{(v) => s2Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {s2Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW</Text>
              <SliderW id="sw2" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="10"
                initialValue="50"
                onDidChange="{(v) => sw2Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sw2Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === Boolean props === -->
        <Card>
          <H2>Boolean props: disabled</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (disabled)</Text>
              <Slider enabled="{false}" initialValue="5" />
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (disabled)</Text>
              <SliderW enabled="{false}" initialValue="5" />
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === ReadOnly === -->
        <Card>
          <H2>ReadOnly</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (readOnly)</Text>
              <Slider readOnly="{true}" initialValue="7" />
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (readOnly)</Text>
              <SliderW readOnly="{true}" initialValue="7" />
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === API: setValue === -->
        <Card var.s4Val="" var.sw4Val="">
          <H2>API: setValue / value</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider</Text>
              <Slider id="s4" minValue="0" maxValue="100"
                initialValue="25"
                onDidChange="{(v) => s4Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {s4Val}</Text>
              <HStack>
                <Button onClick="{s4.setValue(0)}">Set 0</Button>
                <Button onClick="{s4.setValue(50)}">Set 50</Button>
                <Button onClick="{s4.setValue(100)}">Set 100</Button>
              </HStack>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW</Text>
              <SliderW id="sw4" minValue="0" maxValue="100"
                initialValue="25"
                onDidChange="{(v) => sw4Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sw4Val}</Text>
              <HStack>
                <Button onClick="{sw4.setValue(0)}">Set 0</Button>
                <Button onClick="{sw4.setValue(50)}">Set 50</Button>
                <Button onClick="{sw4.setValue(100)}">Set 100</Button>
              </HStack>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === Range slider (multiple thumbs) === -->
        <Card var.s5Val="" var.sw5Val="">
          <H2>Range slider (two thumbs)</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider</Text>
              <Slider id="s5" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="5"
                initialValue="[20,80]"
                onDidChange="{(v) => s5Val = JSON.stringify(v)}" />
              <Text>Value: {s5Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW</Text>
              <SliderW id="sw5" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="5"
                initialValue="[20,80]"
                onDidChange="{(v) => sw5Val = JSON.stringify(v)}" />
              <Text>Value: {sw5Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === Validation status === -->
        <Card>
          <H2>Validation status</H2>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (error)</Text>
              <Slider validationStatus="error" initialValue="3" />
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (error)</Text>
              <SliderW validationStatus="error" initialValue="3" />
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

      </VStack>
    </Page>

    <Page url="/slider-vs-sliderw">
      <VStack padding="2rem" gap="2rem">

        <H1>Slider vs SliderW</H1>

        <Markdown>
These tests show what **SliderW** can do that **Slider** can't.
`SliderNative.tsx` accepts props that the hand-written renderer never forwards.
`wrapComponent` forwards everything automatically, so these "just work."
        </Markdown>

        <!-- === inverted: SliderW only === -->
        <Card var.s6Val="" var.sw6Val="">
          <H2>inverted — only works with SliderW</H2>
          <Markdown>
`SliderNative` accepts an `inverted` prop (from Radix) that reverses direction.
The hand-written **Slider** renderer never forwards it — so it's silently ignored.
**SliderW** forwards all native props automatically.
          </Markdown>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (inverted — ignored)</Text>
              <Slider inverted="{true}" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="10"
                initialValue="70"
                onDidChange="{(v) => s6Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {s6Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (inverted — works)</Text>
              <SliderW inverted="{true}" minValue="0" maxValue="100" step="10"
                initialValue="70"
                onDidChange="{(v) => sw6Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sw6Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === title: native tooltip on hover === -->
        <Card var.s7Val="" var.sw7Val="">
          <H2>title — native HTML tooltip (hover to see)</H2>
          <Markdown>
`SliderNative` spreads `...rest` onto its outer div, so standard HTML
attributes like `title` pass through. The hand-written renderer
never forwards it. Hover each slider to compare.
          </Markdown>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (title — ignored)</Text>
              <Slider title="Pick a temperature" minValue="0" maxValue="100"
                initialValue="50"
                onDidChange="{(v) => s7Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {s7Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
            <VStack>
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (title — hover me!)</Text>
              <SliderW title="Pick a temperature" minValue="0" maxValue="100"
                initialValue="50"
                onDidChange="{(v) => sw7Val = v}" />
              <Text>Value: {sw7Val}</Text>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === tabIndex: keyboard focus order === -->
        <Card>
          <H2>tabIndex — keyboard focus order (press Tab)</H2>
          <Markdown>
Three sliders with tabIndex 3, 2, 1 — so Tab should visit them
in reverse visual order (C, B, A). The hand-written renderer
drops tabIndex, so **Slider** follows default DOM order.
Click below the sliders, then press Tab repeatedly.
          </Markdown>
          <HStack gap="2rem">
            <VStack gap="1rem">
              <Text fontWeight="bold">Slider (tabIndex — ignored)</Text>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>A (tabIndex=3):</Text>
                <Slider tabIndex="3" initialValue="3" />
              </HStack>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>B (tabIndex=2):</Text>
                <Slider tabIndex="2" initialValue="5" />
              </HStack>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>C (tabIndex=1):</Text>
                <Slider tabIndex="1" initialValue="7" />
              </HStack>
            </VStack>
            <VStack gap="1rem">
              <Text fontWeight="bold">SliderW (tabIndex — works: C, B, A)</Text>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>A (tabIndex=3):</Text>
                <SliderW tabIndex="3" initialValue="3" />
              </HStack>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>B (tabIndex=2):</Text>
                <SliderW tabIndex="2" initialValue="5" />
              </HStack>
              <HStack gap="0.5rem">
                <Text>C (tabIndex=1):</Text>
                <SliderW tabIndex="1" initialValue="7" />
              </HStack>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

      </VStack>
    </Page>

  </Pages>
</App>
